			<div class="content" id="post-content-2817772">
									

<p>This comes across as particularly dull and generic. It's stored in a giant cubic cell for no reason. The tests repeat the information we've learned in the Description.</p>
<p>The anomaly is essentially a bog-standard &quot;insanity and then death&quot; effect, with the twist being the common (and difficult to believe) &quot;someone who knows all about the Foundation is using it as a weapon&quot;. The PoI is never made a character or humanised, which might have made this interesting.</p>
<p>The note at the end doesn't tell us anything we haven't already learned (although it also doesn't make sense - SCP-3115/A hasn't been described, so how does the D Class know that the person in the video is /A?). And the note is also too casual - &quot;this guy&quot;, &quot;all such 'deliveries'&quot; - which is noticeable throughout the skip.</p>
<p>So much of this is cliché - I don't see the value here.</p>

